+# FX P&L Report DAG - Updated Schedule
+
+## Summary
+The `fx_pnl_report` DAG has been updated to run on weekdays at 6am New York time and report the **previous business day's** trades.
+
+## Schedule Details
+
+### Execution Times
+- **Frequency**: Weekdays only (Monday-Friday)
+- **Time**: 6:00 AM Eastern Time (EST/EDT)
+  - Translates to 11:00 AM UTC in winter (EST = UTC-5)
+  - Translates to 10:00 AM UTC in summer (EDT = UTC-4)
+- **Note**: The DAG is scheduled at 11:10 AM UTC to account for DST variations
+
+### No Weekend Runs
+- Saturday and Sunday: No execution
+- Next run after Friday is always Monday
+
+## Reporting Logic
+
+### Previous Business Day Rule
+Each run reports the **previous business day**, not the execution date:
+
+| Execution Day | Execution Time (NY) | Reports Data For |
+|---|---|---|
+| Monday 6am | Monday 6:00 AM | Friday |
+| Tuesday 6am | Tuesday 6:00 AM | Monday |
+| Wednesday 6am | Wednesday 6:00 AM | Tuesday |
+| Thursday 6am | Thursday 6:00 AM | Wednesday |
+| Friday 6am | Friday 6:00 AM | Thursday |
+
+### Why Previous Business Day?
+This allows desk heads to pull the report first thing Monday morning (before market open) with complete Friday position data already processed.
+
+## Report Files
+
+### File Naming
+```
+fx_pnl_<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv
+```
+
+Example:
+- Monday 6am run creates: `fx_pnl_2026-01-30.csv` (Friday's data)
+- Tuesday 6am run creates: `fx_pnl_2026-02-02.csv` (Monday's data)
+
+### File Contents
+Columns (unchanged from original):
+```
+desk, trades, notional_usd, pnl_usd
+```
+
+Example output:
+```csv
+desk,trades,notional_usd,pnl_usd
+AMER,4,11300000.00,-30754.98
+APAC,1,4100000.00,19402.98
+EMEA,4,11900000.00,-12479.38
+```
+
+## Implementation Notes
+
+### Time Zone Handling
+- Airflow internally uses UTC for all scheduling
+- The DAG receives execution timestamps in UTC
+- The `build_report()` task converts UTC time to New York time for accurate date calculation
+- The date used to filter trades is always in New York date (not UTC date)
+
+### No Bank Holiday Handling
+As requested, bank holidays are not currently handled. If a Monday is a bank holiday:
+- The DAG still runs at 6am NY time
+- It will still report Friday's trades
+- Consider adding holiday logic in the future if needed
+
+## Data Source
+Source file: `data/fx_trades.csv`
+- Each row has a `trade_date` field (YYYY-MM-DD format, New York date)
+- Trades are aggregated by `desk` (AMER, EMEA, APAC)
+- Report shows count, total notional USD, and total P&L USD per desk
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- File names and CSV structure remain identical to the original DAG
+- Desk heads' Excel pulls will continue to work without modification
+- Only the execution schedule and data date have changed
+
